      "widgets_values": [
        "# H3 REFERENCES REEL · quickstart: the night watch, a reel that keeps a face (the \"Reel: the night watch\" preset)\n# Wiring: picks → Orrery Refs and Orrery Continue; Orrery Refs' ref_N → Reference to Video's ref_image_N-1;\n#   the sampled latent and the decoded clip → Orrery Film · no input image: images 1 and 2 come from the reel\n# REMEMBER: frame 0 as image 1   the first clip's frame 0 (his face) becomes image 1 for every later clip, so\n#   the last clip can come back to his face after two clips that never show it · @KEEPER (image 1) names it\n#   in the prompt from then on · the lamp clip keeps its frame 0 as image 2, a reference for the view from\n#   the top · last frame, frame at 1s · … in clips 4+ (or 4-8, or 4, 6, 7) gives it to those clips only\n# Your own pictures: @NAME (image 3): … in the CAST, and a Load Image into Orrery Refs' image_3\n# Run it: Roll next 3 clips plays the reel · Restart goes back to clip 1 · keep the seed fixed\n@h3 references 16:9 lite 0.6MP\nstyle: live-action, cinematic\ncontext: 22\n$storm = {a rising gale|a heavy sea fog|a thunderstorm rolling in from the sea}\n\nMUSIC: a low, sustained cello drone at a slow tempo\n\nCAST\n@KEEPER (image 1): an old lighthouse keeper, in a yellow oilskin coat and a knitted cap\n\nSCENE the stairs\nSHOT 8s: tracking, slow\n@KEEPER's weathered face is lit by his lantern as he looks up the iron spiral stairs of the lighthouse; then he turns and climbs them while $storm batters the tower.\nSFX: boots ring on iron steps; wind howls against the walls\nEND ON: @KEEPER reaches the top of the lighthouse and looks out over the sea for boats\nREMEMBER: frame 0 as image 1\n\nSCENE the lamp\nSHOT 7s: push in, small, slow\nAt the top, @KEEPER sees a small fishing boat far below, fighting the waves, and the boat turns toward the light.\nSFX: waves crash against the rocks; a distant ship's horn answers\nEND ON: the small boat is fighting the waves\nREMEMBER: frame 0 as image 2\n\nSCENE the ship\nSHOT 8s: arc\nAfter four seconds the camera moves in to a close-up of @KEEPER's face, with a sorrowful expression.\nSFX: waves crash against the rocks; a distant ship's horn answers\n",
