      "title": "orrery",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## orrery · H3 references reel (a reel that keeps a face)\n\nThe night watch: the first clip opens on the keeper's face, and `REMEMBER: frame 0 as image 1` makes that frame image 1 for every later clip, so the last clip can come back to his face in close-up after two clips that never show it; the lamp clip's first frame goes along as image 2, for the view from the top. **No input image is needed**: Orrery Refs fetches the frames from the reel's clips and hands them to Reference to Video, and from the second clip on the prompt names image 1 (`@KEEPER (image 1)`). Clips are chained by **Orrery Continue** / **Orrery Film** as in the reel workflow.\n\nFor pictures of your own, name them in the CAST (`@NAME (image 3): …`) and wire a Load Image into Orrery Refs' `image_3`.\n\nThe **Orrery Prompt** node is the whole of orrery: write in its **Prompt** tab (this workflow opens with a quickstart; **New** has the other modes), roll it in **Test** without queueing, and rate what comes out in **Gallery**: the ratings steer the next rolls. **Roll** in the node queues this graph (next N clips or images: how many runs); what the Save node writes is logged to the gallery with the picks that made it.\n\n- `seed` drives the rolls and the sampler (Random Noise).\n- The model runs through the Orrery Prompt (`model` in, `model` out to the scheduler and the guider): its `LORA:` lines go on the model, and the results under the prompt show the live preview while it samples.\n\n[orrery on GitHub](https://github.com/pyros-projects/ComfyUI-orrery) · [the prompt language](https://github.com/pyros-projects/ComfyUI-orrery/blob/main/docs/dsl.md) · [H3 screenplays](https://github.com/pyros-projects/ComfyUI-orrery/blob/main/docs/h3.md)"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## orrery · H3 references reel (a reel that keeps a face)\n\nThe night watch: the first clip opens on the keeper's face, and `REMEMBER: frame 0 as image 1` makes that frame image 1 for every later clip, so the last clip can come back to his face in close-up after two clips that never show it; the lamp clip's first frame goes along as image 2, for the view from the top. **No input image is needed**: Orrery Refs fetches the frames from the reel's clips and hands them to Reference to Video, and from the second clip on the prompt names image 1 (`@KEEPER (image 1)`). Clips are chained by **Orrery Continue** / **Orrery Film** as in the reel workflow.\n\nFor pictures of your own, name them in the CAST (`@NAME (image 3): …`) and wire a Load Image into Orrery Refs' `image_3`.\n\nThe **Orrery Prompt** node is the whole of orrery: write in its **Prompt** tab (this workflow opens with a quickstart; **New** has the other modes), roll it in **Test** without queueing, and rate what comes out in **Gallery**: the ratings steer the next rolls. **Roll** in the node queues this graph (next N clips or images: how many runs); what the Save node writes is logged to the gallery with the picks that made it.\n\n- `seed` drives the rolls and the sampler (Random Noise).\n- `LORA:` lines come out on `lora_stack`, for a loader with a `lora_stack` input (LoraManager, Efficiency …), which is not part of this core-nodes workflow.\n\n[orrery on GitHub](https://github.com/pyros-projects/ComfyUI-orrery) · [the prompt language](https://github.com/pyros-projects/ComfyUI-orrery/blob/main/docs/dsl.md) · [H3 screenplays](https://github.com/pyros-projects/ComfyUI-orrery/blob/main/docs/h3.md)"
      },
